{"version": 1, "sourceSha256": "ca87e8943384461e12db7b52ca528b1a356b42b008c7457e804bfc87d29aeb28", "documents": [{"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}, {"id": "offline-ca87e8943384461e12db", "filename": "26- Part C.mp3", "sha256": "ca87e8943384461e12db7b52ca528b1a356b42b008c7457e804bfc87d29aeb28", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-5/ca87e8943384461e12db7b52ca528b1a356b42b008c7457e804bfc87d29aeb28.mp3", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/ca87e8943384461e12db7b52ca528b1a356b42b008c7457e804bfc87d29aeb28.json", "format": "mp3", "role": "recording"}], "units": [{"id": "jahshan-1GGvwrRDKJF-vJBPn8f2KapaUhjRD4voj-C-0", "label": "Jahshan set 26 · Part C", "part": "C", "sourceSha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "pages": [292, 293, 294, 295], "questions": [{"number": 31, "prompt": "How did the young patient called David react to the amputation of his leg?\nA He felt he was now excluded from normal life.\nB He compared it to the experience of a relative dying.\nC He resented his inability to take part in physical activities.", "sourcePage": 292, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 297, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 32, "prompt": "What does Dr Sands suggest about pain in a missing or ‘phantom’ limb?\nA Under-reporting by patients makes it hard to know how frequent it is.\nB The discomfort can generally be traced to a physical cause.\nC The problem affects far fewer patients than in the past.", "sourcePage": 292, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "A", "page": 297, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 33, "prompt": "Some patients feel that their missing limb is still attached but\nA would cause pain if they used it.\nB is fixed in a strange position.\nC has increased in size.", "sourcePage": 292, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 297, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 34, "prompt": "Dr Sands’ current treatment trial includes people who have\nA reacted badly to previous treatments.\nB failed to respond to any form of medication.\nC reported pain levels that impact on their daily lives.", "sourcePage": 293, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "C", "page": 297, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 35, "prompt": "In Dr Sands’ current trial, patients are\nA helped to come to terms with the loss of a limb emotionally.\nshown how to manage a computer-operated prosthetic limb.\nB\nC made to move a simulation of the missing limb in their minds.", "sourcePage": 293, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "C", "page": 297, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 36, "prompt": "Dr Sands feels one advantage of the trial group’s treatment is that\nA its effects are long-lasting.\nB it can be used by patients after discharge.\nC it helps certain patients to become almost pain-free.\nNow look at extract two.\n\nExtract 2: Questions 37-42\nYou hear a dermatologist called Dr Jake Cooper talking about a skin condition called Hidradenitis Suppurativa (HS).\nYou now have 90 seconds to read questions 37-42.", "sourcePage": 293, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 297, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 37, "prompt": "When describing the condition known as HS, Dr Cooper suggests that it\nA is fairly common so should be more accurately diagnosed.\nB would be better understood if it presented more uniformly.\nC may be incorrectly treated due to misinformation from patients.\nP L", "sourcePage": 294, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "A", "page": 297, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 38, "prompt": "Dr Cooper explains that one cause of HS may be blocked hair follicles resulting from\nA shaving of the affected area.\nB the overuse of deodorants.\nthe effects of smoking.\nC", "sourcePage": 294, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "C", "page": 297, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 39, "prompt": "When describing the case of a patient called Sophie, Dr Cooper suggests that\nA HS has a tendency to get progressively worse.\nB diagnosis of HS may require a full patient history.\nC a multiple treatment approach is often required for HS.", "sourcePage": 294, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 297, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 40, "prompt": "Dr Cooper says that those treating patients with HS should be aware that the condition\nA may recur after disappearing for many years.\nB may be triggered by an episode of depression.\nC may become increasingly difficult to treat over time.", "sourcePage": 294, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "A", "page": 297, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 41, "prompt": "When discussing a patient called Emily, Dr Cooper suggests that her mother’s attitude\nA reflected a lack of sympathy and understanding.\nB led to a delay in confirming the correct diagnosis.\nC may have contributed to the severity of the symptoms.", "sourcePage": 295, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "A", "page": 297, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 42, "prompt": "When discussing the treatment of HS sufferers, Dr Cooper recommends they should\nA eat healthy foods such as brown bread.\nrestrict their intake of dairy products.\nB\nC avoid all types of alcoholic drinks.\nYou now have two minutes to check your answers.\nTHAT IS THE END OF THE LISTENING TEST", "sourcePage": 295, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 297, "source": {"id": "offline-51c74510842bc49d5bab", "filename": "Listening Jahshan OET Collection.pdf", "sha256": "51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/51c74510842bc49d5babacdaf2a5b241a20e90979e03a98534645f748a7120fa.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}], "skills": ["listening"], "recordings": ["ca87e8943384461e12db7b52ca528b1a356b42b008c7457e804bfc87d29aeb28"], "answerSources": [], "matchEvidence": "Exact original recording SHA-256 in the verified Jahshan collection"}]}
